        theme:smallholder-agriculture,
        theme:sustainable-agriculture,
        theme:sustainable-water-management,
        theme:waste-management,
        theme:water-sanitation-and-hygiene-wash ;
    skos:definition """Describes the type(s) of technologies provisioned, enabled, or adopted by an organization or their clients or communities served, during a reporting period. 

Choose all that apply: 
- Information and Communication Technology
   - Internet of Things (IoT)
   - Artificial Intelligence (AI)
   - Big Data Analytics
   - Blockchain
- Renewable Energy Technology:
   - Solar Power
   - Wind Power
   - Hydropower
- Climate Technology:
   - Precision Agriculture
   - Early warning systems
   - Remote Sensing
   - Biodiversity Monitoring
   - Waste Management
   - Water Treatment
   - Recycling
   - Adaptation and resilience
- Transportation Technology:
   - Electric Vehicles (EVs)
   - Autonomous Vehicles
- Healthcare Technology:
   - Telemedicine
   - Medical Imaging
   - Biotechnology
- Construction and Infrastructure Technology:
   - 3D Printing
   - Smart Buildings
- Financial Technology (Fintech):
   - Mobile Payments
   - Peer-to-Peer Lending
- Educational Technology (EdTech):
   - Learning Management Systems (LMS)
   - Virtual Reality (VR) and Augmented Reality (AR)
   - Carbon Capture and Storage (CCS) Technologies:
   - Direct Air Capture
   - Carbon Sequestration
- Other (Describe)"""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://iris.thegiin.org/taxonomy> ;
    skos:notation "PD2348" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Technology Type"@en .

